# Dead Cells (PPSA15552): full-render fresh-save route to first gameplay.
# Unlike reach-first-gameplay.pad, this does not depend on a renderer warmup making
# guest startup run ahead. Full rendering can reduce pad polls below 1 Hz, so
# every menu action is held across several polls with a release gap between it
# and the next action. Circle remains held through the slow full-render parse and skippable opening;
# it deliberately outlives the current snapshot timeout so host throughput cannot expire the skip.
# Late Cross windows overlap that hold (the replay backend ORs active entries). They preserve the
# opening skip while supplying distinct Jump presses when a slow parse exposes that tutorial only
# after the original menu-confirm windows have ended. A final left-stick hold lets either observed landing
# position fall to and settle against the same lower boundary before the evidence window.
40-48:cross
52-60:cross
64-72:cross
76-84:cross
88-96:cross
100-108:cross
112-120:cross
124-300:circle
128-136:cross
140-148:cross
152-160:cross
164-172:cross
176-184:cross
188-240:left-stick-left
